WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
<b>Gama Gama Aquarium To Close</b>

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
<b>After 48 years of being a fixture in the community, 
the Aquarium will close at the end of August.</b>

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.840
Good morning.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.120
K-Kuuya-san.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.640
Were we back-washing the main tank today?

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.520
We did that yesterday, remember?

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.990
Right, we did.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.560
Kukuru.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.180
Hey. Kukuru.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.090
Your eyebrows are furrowed.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.410
You look scary.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:57.840
Oh, shoot!

00:01:58.450 --> 00:01:59.640
Are you okay?

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.040
I was thinking of ways 
to attract more visitors,

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.920
but I can't come up with anything good.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.520
What have you come up with so far?

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.920
A fish cosplay festival.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.030
What are we, in kindergarten?

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:11.770
An all-night aquarium.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.020
I'm not doing overtime.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.150
Haunted aquarium for summer chills.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.380
So random.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.140
I have to do something, though!

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.950
Kukuru, wrinkles!

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:28.120
Nothing beats shochu-infused
ice pops after work.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.950
You have them during work, too.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.610
Don't be so anal.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.640
I see.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.420
Ice cream.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.050
Want some, Fuuka-chan?

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.100
No thanks, but I appreciate it.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.930
How about some cold sweets?

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.180
Sweets?

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.950
Gama Gama doesn't sell any food, right?

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.560
I thought people might enjoy it 
if we sold some sweets.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.580
They might, but...

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.060
I don't know about having
people come for the snacks.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.420
I'd be up for sweets.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.960
Umi-yan, you just want some 
for yourself, don't you?

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:59.700
Let's give that a try.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:05.120
If the guests like it, 
it might help draw more traffic.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.870
I want to try everything we can 
for Operation Summer Break.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:10.820
Yeah!

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.880
But who?

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.640
Who else?

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.040
Please, Udon-chan, request of a lifetime.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.040
Again?

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.240
How many requests of a lifetime has it been?

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.760
I'm begging you!

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.280
<b>Kamee Diner</b>

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.550
I see.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:31.520
So you want some cold sweets 
for the summer.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.200
I want to see if we can win
them over with original sweets.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.650
I'm sure you can come up with
something really delicious, Udon-chan.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.120
Leave it to five-star chef Teruya Tsukimi!

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:48.810
Or so I'd like to say, but I actually
haven't really made sweets that often.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:49.740
No way.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:50.660
Really?

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:54.480
I only learned to cook by watching my mom.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.640
Tsukimi!

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:57.800
Could you get me 
some braised pork belly?

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.000
Mango pork belly?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.920
No, a normal one.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.380
Fruit pork belly is blasphemy.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.220
It's against our family tradition.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.180
Right, her mom doesn't like sweet stuff.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.400
What should we do?

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.390
We were counting on Udon-chan.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.520
I might not be able to make something
proper like a pâtissier could,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.400
but if that's all right, 
I want to give it a shot.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.320
Really?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.780
I'm rarely going to have
an opportunity to try it out.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.530
And I want to add more to my repertoire.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.720
Thanks, Udon-chan!

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.200
We're counting on you.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.180
What's taking so long?

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:29.980
I'm still waiting.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.940
Okay, okay, coming.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:39.630
<b>Kamee Diner</b>

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.360
Later, Tsukimi-chan!

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.630
Get home safe.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.640
<b>Special Original</b>

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.640
<b>Cold Sweets</b>

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.640
<b>Ice cream</b>

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.640
<b>Cake</b>

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.640
<b>Tarts</b>

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.640
<b>Yogurt</b>

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.640
<b>Crepes</b>

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.640
<b>Sherbet</b>

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.060
Cakes would be good.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:46.640
So would tarts and crepes.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.210
Original sweets, huh?

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.560
Thanks for cleaning.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:13.020
Could you clean the protein
skimmer once you're done?

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.000
Got it.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.150
I have a meeting with Udon-chan soon.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.750
She agreed to it?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.840
Yeah.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.130
She said she'll try to come
up with some sweets.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.540
Yeah?

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.220
I hope it works out.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.200
Hey!

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.280
Udon-chan!

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.470
Welcome!

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.850
Well, let's begin our first sweets meeting.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.860
I have Proposals A through G.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.190
Where do you want to start?

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.680
You came up with all that in one night?

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.860
Let's start from A, then.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.550
Okay, here we go.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:49.450
Proposal A is an Okinawan Special Parfait!

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.450
<b>Proposal A</b>

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.450
<b>Okinawan Special Parfait</b>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.450
<b>Hibiscus</b>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.450
<b>Mango jelly</b>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.450
<b>Mint</b>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.450
<b>Banana</b>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.450
<b>Starfruit</b>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.450
<b>Orange</b>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.450
<b>Pineapple</b>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.450
<b>Kiwi</b>

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.450
<b>Mango</b>

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:56.120
Try our cold, sweet, tropical
parfait full of our local fruits.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.470
A parfait, huh?

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:58.960
That looks so good.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:04.490
We make a café space in front of the tanks 
and set up a rattan table and sofa.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:08.070
Have a taste of an
out-of-the-ordinary overseas resort!

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:10.720
I bet it'll be popular.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.200
I think it'll create some buzz.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.590
It'll create buzz, become famous, 
and bring lots of guests!

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:17.450
Sounds good.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:20.840
Don't you think a café might be 
too big of a project, though?

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.590
How much do we have in our budget?

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:23.610
5,000 yen?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:24.750
Eh?

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.090
That's never going to work.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.490
I figured.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.030
Hm...

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:34.240
Considering all our constraints, 
the most viable one would be...

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:38.250
Setting up a food stall here 
and selling original ice cream.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.120
That sounds good!

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:43.690
I think we can borrow a stall 
through Karin-chan.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.880
That's probably the most realistic.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.640
You might be right.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.710
All right, ice cream! Agreed?

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:50.970
Agreed!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.570
Great!

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:54.850
Let's get going, then.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:55.990
Huh?

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:57.140
Go where?

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:03.690
If we're going to make ice cream, 
we've got to try some first.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.060
What should we get?

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.950
I can't decide.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.290
I'm sticking with vanilla.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.200
I'll have pineapple chocolate.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:17.710
A triple scoop with red bean matcha,
avocado nut, and cheese pistachio.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.230
Time to eat.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:28.460
Yum!

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.340
It's so rich and creamy.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.180
It has a complex taste.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.750
The nuts don't all taste the same.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:37.790
I see.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:41.230
They're blending several kinds of nuts.

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.440
She's a diligent researcher.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.760
She's always been that way.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:46.890
In cooking class in elementary school,

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:49.230
Udon-chan's group came up 
with all kinds of ideas.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:52.080
She made stuff that you
might get at a restaurant.

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.210
There are infinite possibilities in cooking.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:58.840
Even with the same ingredients, 
you can get something totally different

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.650
if you cook it differently 
or use different spices.

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:03.390
I'm in bliss whenever I try different things

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:06.300
and come up with something 
completely unexpected!

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:10.260
I'm glad we asked Udon-chan.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:14.940
I always end up accepting 
all of Kukuru's "requests of a lifetime."

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:17.790
I really don't remember, though.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:20.140
I know. You tend to forget 
when you're the one asking.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:21.360
Right?

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.480
Like, "Udon-chan, request of a lifetime: 
Can I borrow your eraser?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.040
Can you come with me to the restroom?"

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.100
Stuff like that.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.180
That's just a waste of requests.

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:31.640
What's wrong with that?

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:32.490
Sheesh.

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:40.300
Okay, I'm going to go check out 
a few more ice cream shops.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:41.180
See you.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.400
Thanks.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:45.880
We should head back, too.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:46.740
Yeah.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.630
<b>We're on Penstagram!</b>

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.630
<b>Follow us for a free topping!</b>

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.710
Penstagram, huh?

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:55.530
What? What's up?

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:00.750
All the aquariums these days 
are on social media.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:03.320
I've been wanting 
to get Gama Gama on, too.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:04.510
It's useful, right?

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.350
It makes it easy to advertise.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.980
Were you on social media?

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.150
I'm not anymore, but I was back then.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.160
Huh.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.490
Tell me how, then.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:14.360
Okay!

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.950
What makes Gama Gama special?

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.900
Hopefully we can get that across.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.770
What makes Gama Gama special?

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.520
There.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:33.760
Now...

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.130
I'm in the middle of work.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:39.090
Be a man and stop whining.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.220
I don't want to put my face online.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.380
Help me out!

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.730
Kukuru-chan, you here?

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.230
Take a picture of this one, too.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:53.920
Frogfish!

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.340
My personal favorite.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:57.600
It's so cute!

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.110
Yeah, I like that.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:04.620
That's a really good photo.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.670
I-Is it?

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:10.640
It'd be nice if we had some photos 
that show off the vibe in the aquarium, too.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:12.600
The "vibe," huh?

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:14.210
Huh?

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.850
Do you know him?

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:16.810
Yeah.

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:19.560
He comes every year in the summer.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:20.720
Every year?

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:23.340
Ever since I was little.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:25.350
For that long?

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:28.820
He must love the aquarium.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.280
<b>Kudaka Karin</b>

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.280
<b>Cell phone</b>

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:35.280
<b>Send a message</b>

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.280
<b>Remind me later</b>

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.530
<b>Kamee Diner</b>

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:43.410
I hate to tell you this, but I don't think 
you can do homemade ice cream.

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:46.410
We can't?

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:49.920
<b>Sweets Rhapsody</b>

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.920
Ice cream production permits?

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:53.960
Yeah.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.740
According to Food Safety Law,

00:10:55.740 --> 00:11:01.930
you need an production permit 
to sell ice cream indoors or at stalls.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:02.830
Do you have one?

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:04.040
No.

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.430
But can't we just submit a request?

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:09.200
Apparently, they reject most requests.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:13.400
A shop is one thing, but it's hard
to maintain food safety outdoors.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.700
No way...

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:17.190
Ice cream would never work!

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:19.210
You knew, Mom?

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.070
It's common sense.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:27.330
People think food is easy, 
but licenses and permits aren't easy to get.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.490
Why?

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:30.040
Why wouldn't it be?

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.320
It's going in people's mouths.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:35.360
You could be putting their lives in danger.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:39.130
Ma'am, do you know of anything else 
that we could get a permit for?

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:41.710
Let's see...

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:43.340
How about shaved ice?

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:44.680
Shaved ice?

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:48.860
You still need a permit, but it should be 
a lot easier to get than for dairy.

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:52.040
Udon-chan?

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.520
I'll do it.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.270
I'm going home to research shaved ice!

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.100
Take care of the shop for me!

00:11:58.850 --> 00:11:59.930
Wait, don't leave!

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.020
Tsukimi!

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.070
So fluffy!

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:10.120
It's so good!

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.070
Right?

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:14.840
You leave the ice out of the freezer 
for a while before you shave it,

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:16.600
and that makes it fluffy!

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:18.800
That's our Udon-chan.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:21.600
Are we using this for the shop, though?

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:22.800
Of course not.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:26.390
Karin-chan's getting a hold of 
a commercial machine for us.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:29.770
Huh, aren't you having any, Kuuya-san?

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:30.970
I'm good.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.990
I hate brain freeze.

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:35.210
I'll have it, then.

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:41.030
Oh yeah, you should make
shochu shaved ice, too.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:44.110
That's just plain shochu 
with water once it melts.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:44.910
Denied.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.740
We're on the job. What are you thinking?

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.500
<b>Kamee Diner</b>

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.000
<b>Closed</b>

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:57.400
Done!

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.060
What's the matter?

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:05.800
I never see you looking so serious.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.450
Oh?

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:11.340
That looks pretty boring.

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:12.140
What does?

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:15.180
It's kinda dull, especially for you.

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:16.900
What can you do, though, huh?

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:19.560
There isn't much you can do with shaved ice.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>Shaved Ice</b>

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>Strawberry</b>

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>Mango</b>

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>Lemon</b>

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>Melon</b>

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>Ramune</b>

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>Grape</b>

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>Coffee</b>

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:22.040
Anyone could do this.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.150
What's that supposed to mean?

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:28.910
I don't like it, personally, but what gave you 
the idea to make mango pork belly?

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:34.360
Oh, right.

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:36.290
Okay!

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:42.050
<b>Closed</b>

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:40.750
Huh?

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.050
Are they not open yet?

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.170
Good evening!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:45.940
Udon-chan.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:47.680
Welcome.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:50.440
You haven't even opened shop. 
What are you doing?

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:53.060
Preparing for tomorrow, of course.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:57.520
Man, I never knew living things 
were so hard to draw.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:01.360
I've been so eager about making
the shaved ice shop happen,

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.280
and I've been overthinking it.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:05.780
I guess I can freewheel it more.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:10.160
I think it should be something 
people can get only at Gama Gama.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.680
So what's this?

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:14.580
Yeah.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.610
I wanted you guys to help draw.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:25.510
Do what's right, 
and everything will work out.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.340
Please give us luck!

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:31.220
There!

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:40.150
Good thing the health center agreed, huh?

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:41.290
Yeah.

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:43.070
That's one less thing to worry about.

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:46.110
Why did we have to get dragged out?

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.040
No complaining.

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:50.740
We have permission from the director.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:53.740
<b>Welcome to Gama Gama Aquarium</b>

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:09.010
<b><i>Gobiodon okinawae</i></b>

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.800
Kukuru!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.200
Welcome.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.500
Thank you for coming every year.

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:20.780
It's almost over, huh?

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.920
I read the newspaper.

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:27.030
What a shame that it's going away.

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:31.140
It's not for sure yet.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.810
I see.

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:39.910
I have some very special memories here.

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:42.030
At Gama Gama?

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:48.090
A long time ago, when I was still young, 
I lost my older brother.

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:55.400
After I grew up, I started a business 
and worked really hard to honor my brother.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:16:01.520
But things didn't work out, 
and we had to close.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:07.770
That's when I happened to come by this aquarium, 
when it was brand new.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:11.370
And I saw my dead brother.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:17.210
He cheered me up and got me out of my rut.

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:20.200
I mean... I didn't actually
get to talk to him.

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:22.790
It just felt like that.

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:29.280
But thanks to that, I got back on my feet 
and succeeded in building a new business.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:35.770
Since then, I've been coming here every year 
in an attempt to meet with my brother again.

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:37.800
He didn't show up this year, either.

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:42.480
Sorry to be such a downer.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.480
No.

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:45.180
Thank you.

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:49.480
I'm really happy that this place 
is special to you.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:54.900
<i>A precious, special...</i>

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.460
Please come back next year.

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.810
I'm going to make sure it stays open.

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:48.540
I'll be looking forward to it.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:00.450
<i>Gama Gama is a special place.</i>

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:03.140
<i>Some other people think so, too.</i>

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.880
<i>It's not just me.</i>

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:10.460
<b>Shaved Ice</b>

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:10.460
Welcome!

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:14.460
Weekend exclusive Gama Gama 
special shaved ice!

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:17.340
Wow, it's all set up.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:20.220
She worked me way too hard.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.220
<b>Gama Gama Aquarium Original Shaved Ice</b>

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.220
<b>Special Menu</b>

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.220
<b>African Penguin</b>

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.220
<b>Chinese Box Turtle</b>

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.220
<b>Clownfish</b>

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.220
<b>Yellowtail Fusilier</b>

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.220
<b>Sunburst Butterflyfish</b>

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:22.350
What's this?

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:27.440
Choose one, and I'll make you 
my best shaved ice ever.

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:29.150
I want the Clownfish.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.440
African Penguin!

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:31.850
Gotcha!

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:43.820
Here you are!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.450
Woah, awesome!

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.880
So cool!

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:48.060
What's that?

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:49.080
Can I see?

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:54.000
That's a unique idea, 
using animal names for orders.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.460
Udon-chan came up with it.

00:19:56.900 --> 00:20:00.220
So that people would have good
memories of the aquarium.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:03.260
She said she wanted to make something 
people would never forget.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.180
Um, I know it's not on the menu, but...

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:08.850
Could you do frogfish?

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:12.230
Okay, I'll give it a try!

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:18.570
There you are!

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:19.790
Holy...

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:21.190
Wow!

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:23.280
Isn't that...

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:25.180
The fish that's Umi-yan fave.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.950
It doesn't matter what brings them in.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:32.550
As long as people take interest in sea life.

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:35.460
Yeah, I guess.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:38.750
We should get back to work, too.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:39.460
Yeah.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:43.140
Try some Gama Gama Aquarium shaved ice!

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:15.930
<b>Kamee Diner</b>

00:22:14.570 --> 00:22:15.930
Thank you so much!

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:19.360
I've had so much help from you, Udon-chan.

00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:20.560
Thanks. Seriously!

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:22.360
It's fine.

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:24.570
I'm having fun, too.

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:26.700
The shaved ice is really popular.

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:28.630
It's on Penstagram, too.

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:28.740
<b>I didn't know what to expect from Gama Gama Aquarium original 
Chinese Box Turtle Shaved Ice, but it was actually really turtle-y lol</b>

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:30.530
<b>Yellowtail fusilier be like, "Can you eat me?" 
And I did. It was delicious.</b>

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:31.530
<b>Look what they're selling at the local aquarium! 
They got the butterflyfish patterns down perfectly. My kid loved it, too.</b>

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:37.520
I hope we can keep getting more customers.

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:38.300
Yeah.

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:39.280
Let's do this!

00:22:39.280 --> 00:22:41.040
Me, too!

00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:49.440
Nah, I was just thinking. I should study
more for when I have my own shop.

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:50.680
Your own shop?

00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:53.630
I can do whatever I want, 
if I have my own shop.

00:22:53.630 --> 00:22:55.850
I can come up with
my own original menu items

00:22:55.850 --> 00:22:57.930
and do the interior exactly how I want it.

00:22:57.930 --> 00:22:59.960
There's so much to dream about.

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:00.860
Okay!

00:23:00.860 --> 00:23:03.040
I'll be your first regular customer.

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:04.080
Tsukimi?

00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:05.940
Mango pork belly over here.

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:06.990
Okay.

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.440
Mango pork belly, right away.

00:23:08.890 --> 00:23:09.740
Huh?

00:23:09.740 --> 00:23:11.450
Not normal pork belly?

00:23:11.920 --> 00:23:14.450
Hurry up, before I change my mind.

00:23:14.450 --> 00:23:15.830
Here you are!

00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:21.770
Yeesh!

00:23:21.770 --> 00:23:23.270
It's so sweet.

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:26.670
You're never going 
to have your own shop like this.

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:28.170
Y-You were listening?

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:30.250
You're so loud.

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:31.610
Of course I could hear you!

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:34.870
Come on! I'm so embarrassed.
